WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.258 --> 00:00:03.091
(violins playing)

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.650
- [Tiffany] My mom is
significantly older than me,

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.580
and she always says, she's like,

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.750
"This is just one of those
things that in my lifetime,

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.233
"I just never thought I'd see."

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.130
The City of South Fulton Municipal Court

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.210
is the only court system
in the entire country

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.123
that's run entirely by
African American women.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.573
(orchestral music)

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:33.193
- The City of South Fulton
is Georgia's newest city.

00:00:34.555 --> 00:00:37.070
It was started in 2017.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.780
We became a city with a large
African American population.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.990
One of the largest in the country.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:46.410
It is a city that is
made up of urban, rural,

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.020
and suburban communities,
and I truly think

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.763
this is one of the best
little places in America.

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.580
- The mayor appointed me first.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.610
And then I know you need a
solicitor and a public defender.

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.150
Then, I had to go about
selecting a court administrator.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.430
She, along with myself,
hired the rest of the staff.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.840
So that's kind of how it came about.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.560
- I had the first realization
of the specialness

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.610
of our court and the first response that

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:13.742
I have was like, oh, black girl magic.

00:01:13.742 --> 00:01:16.575
(violins playing)

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.740
- [Guard] All right, and if
you all have any cell phones,

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.120
please put cell phone on off.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.000
- Oftentimes, particularly
for African Americans,

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.933
people feel railroaded by the system.

00:01:31.025 --> 00:01:33.110
A municipal court is often
people's first interaction

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:34.620
with the judicial system.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.000
So it's my position that
we have to get it right,

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.310
because we can change the
perception of the system

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.910
if they have a personal
experience that's counter to that.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.610
Counter to what they perceived
and what they've heard.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.690
And so you know, in South Fulton,

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:48.270
we're not gonna be light on crime.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.330
But we're gonna make sure that
your rights are protected.

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:51.230
I'm sorry, hold on.

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:54.460
Now you want me to hear you,
so you gotta raise your voice

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.670
up so that I can hear you.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:58.540
We believe in being a model for what

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:01.910
a municipal court in a
progressive city looks like.

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:05.427
- All rise, the City of
South Fulton Municipal Court

00:02:05.427 --> 00:02:06.920
is now in session.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.100
Honorable Tiffany Carter
Sellers is the judge presiding.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.960
- One of the things I
think makes our court

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.900
particularly unique is
how we treat people.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.100
We try to take our time to educate people.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.920
So when they pre-try a case with me

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.410
or they're present before the judge,

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.740
they really get information

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.040
about why they are pleading guilty.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.840
We're not just saying
go do community service.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.270
We're saying do community
service within our community.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:29.950
Pre-trial was your opportunity to speak

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:32.440
with me about your case
and come to a resolution.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:34.630
- The law does not require that the person

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.120
is appointed a public defender

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.620
for their first appearance here.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:40.340
I mean in 2018 in a civilized society,

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.690
we just can do it better.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:45.800
And so the city council
has been very gracious

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.530
in providing the funding necessary

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:50.370
to be able to have our public defenders

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.440
available whenever someone is arrested

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.730
for their first appearance here.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.740
Particularly in municipal
courts it's uncommon,

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.260
and so the dynamic is
absolutely different.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.993
This was my opportunity to
operate as a model court.

00:03:02.899 --> 00:03:06.360
To think that we are
kind of the first court

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.720
run completely by African American women

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.040
is really heartwarming.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.680
It's a lot of, I can't
believe it's taken 'til 2018.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:14.980
Because I think for centuries
African American women

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.990
have just done some outstanding things.

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:19.790
I'm glad that we're leading the way

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:22.570
in showing people the
excellence that can occur.

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:24.110
I'm an eternal optimist, particularly

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:26.360
when it comes to the
criminal justice system.

00:03:28.464 --> 00:03:30.631
(chiming)

